WEBVTT

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.332
Game!

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:11.503
Why don't we make it
interesting this time?

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.239
Let's add some table stakes.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.110
What kind of stakes?

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.945
I don't know.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.143
Mmm...

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.152
a couple of replicator rations,
maybe?

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.153
Don't do it, Harry.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.154
He's hustling you.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.213
Wait a minute.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:27.249
Are you saying
he deliberately let me win?

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.163
That would be dishonest, Harry.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:33.889
I won that game...

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.400
and I'll beat you again.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:38.097
How many rations
are you willing to bet on that?

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:40.606
Come on, Harry.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.868
Go for it.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.136
A week's worth.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.274
Harry, Harry, Harry.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.475
Never, ever play with anyone...

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.915
not even your best friend...

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.145
if he says,
"Let's make it interesting."

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.216
Now, you want a little action?

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.917
I'll give you a little action.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.187
How about
an honest game of chance?

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.693
Never play with anyone...

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.855
even your best friend...
if he offers you

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.457
"an honest game of chance,"
Harry.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:10.060
One replicator ration
is all it takes to play

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.094
and the only thing
you have to do to win

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.730
is pick a number.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.297
Just predict

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.865
what the radiogenic
particle count will be

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.707
at 1200 hours tomorrow,

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.373
and if you hit,
the pot is yours...

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.349
minus a small handling fee
for the bank, of course.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.784
I'll take a piece of that.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.980
Harry, get a padd.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.454
Take down
these names and numbers.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.218
I'm in, too.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.417
Lewis... 2100.

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:34.518
I'll back that bet up.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.550
Rogers...

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:41.528
Ensign Hogan, still no luck
with the warp drive?

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.195
No, Lieutenant.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.363
The manifold just won't fire up.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:46.997
We've finally narrowed it down

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:50.668
to some kind of a problem
in EPS Conduit 141.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.177
Was there any indication
yesterday

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:53.338
that there was something wrong?

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.848
Suder was monitoring
the EPS flow in the CCF.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:59.078
He says everything was fine.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.584
Well, I guess we'll just
have to get in there

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.648
and track it down.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.736
Happy Kal Rekk, Mr. Vulcan.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:26.574
The holiday of Kal Rekk
is not for two weeks.

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.774
But it's the Kal Rekk season.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.783
There is no Kal Rekk season.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:34.685
Kal Rekk is a day of atonement,
solitude and silence.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.484
Atonement.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:38.252
Solitude.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.589
All your Vulcan holidays
are the same.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.959
I've been doing some research.
I know.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.362
Why would you
need to do research

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.365
on Vulcan holidays?

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.128
It's part of my job
as morale officer.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:50.932
Morale is irrelevant
to a Vulcan.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.937
Oh, please!

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.131
There's no one on this ship

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.266
requires my services
more than you do.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:03:00.437
I will not rest
until I see you smile.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.311
Then you will not rest.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.940
I don't suppose
you've ever heard

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.314
of the Vulcan Rumarie?

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.582
The Rumarie is
an ancient pagan festival.

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:14.082
Full of barely clothed
Vulcan men and women,

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:18.894
covered in slippery Rillan
grease, chasing one another.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:22.299
That has not been observed
for a millennium.

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:24.200
Well, it's time
to bring it back.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:27.434
Lieutenant Tuvok, report
to Engineering immediately.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.065
Acknowledged.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.900
I've been thinking
of a Rumarie theme

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:33.207
for the Mess Hall next week...

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.975
lots of high-fat, greasy foods,

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.174
and if people want
to take off their clothes

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.241
and chase one another...

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:41.253
well, it certainly wouldn't
hurt morale around here.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.658
Is there a problem,
Lieutenant?

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.514
98 percent of his body suffered
third-degree plasma burns.

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:54.987
If the circuit hadn't failed,
he would have been vaporized.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:57.147
It appeared that Mr. Darwin
had entered the conduit

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.920
to repair a faulty circuit
when the accident occurred.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.256
A perfectly good theory.

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:03.091
Unfortunately, it's wrong.

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.292
This contusion is the result

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.701
of a hard blow
to the back of the skull.

00:06:11.738 --> 00:06:14.400
Perhaps he fell and hit
his head in the conduit.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.806
The coup-contrecoup
pattern of breakage

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:18.333
should tell us whether the blow

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:21.074
is a result of a moving head
hitting a stationary object

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:23.776
or a moving object
hitting a stationary head.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:26.683
In this case, the pattern
clearly indicates the latter.

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:30.052
I'm sorry to report
Crewman Darwin was murdered.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:38.956
At first glance,
there is no obvious motive.

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:41.898
Crewman Darwin didn't have
any known enemies on board.

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:44.903
I've been looking over
his Starfleet record.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.495
His training instructor
recommended him

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:47.972
as an officer's candidate.

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:50.271
He turned it down
to come with us.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:52.243
He has three sisters back home.

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:54.212
Sorry I'm late.

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:56.147
These are the duty logs
from last night.

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:58.377
Lon Suder was the only one
in Engineering

00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:00.283
when Frank Darwin came on duty.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.111
Something wrong?

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:05.681
No, not really.

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:08.125
I've just never been
comfortable with Suder.

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:09.128
That's all.

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:10.424
It's not like he ever
did anything wrong,

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:11.521
it's just...

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:15.193
As a Maquis, he did what he had
to do a little too well.

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.099
As in?

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:18.831
As in killing Cardassians.

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.668
I don't recall observing
anything unusual

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.197
about Mr. Suder's behavior
while I was on your ship.

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:25.073
You weren't with him in battle.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:27.238
Around us, he was the quietest

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.544
most unassuming guy
you'll ever meet.

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:31.243
Typical Betazoid.

00:07:31.284 --> 00:07:32.615
Kept to himself.

00:07:32.652 --> 00:07:33.710
I never knew much about him.

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:36.620
In the Maquis,
we didn't ask for resumes.

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:38.487
We needed all the help
we could get.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:40.389
A lot us were doing
what we were doing

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:41.757
to protect our families,

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:43.728
but Suder had his own reasons.

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:46.391
I wish I could tell you
what they were.

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:48.832
In combat, there was
something in his eyes.

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:51.666
Maybe he had something personal
against Cardassians.

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:54.070
Sometimes I had
to pull him back...

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.937
stop him from going too far.

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:57.738
And once or twice when I did,

00:07:57.777 --> 00:07:59.972
he looked at me
with those cold eyes

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:01.172
and I just knew,

00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:03.910
he was this far away
from killing me.

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:06.644
I find it curious
that none of this was included

00:08:06.686 --> 00:08:08.745
in your initial
crew evaluation, Commander.

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:11.188
I don't put down hunches
or bad feelings

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:13.317
in my crew evaluations,
Lieutenant.

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:15.190
A Vulcan should appreciate that.

00:08:15.228 --> 00:08:16.320
Considering the fact

00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:19.126
that your Maquis crew
included malcontents,

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:21.463
outlaws and mercenaries,

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:23.332
I believe it would
have been appropriate.

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:25.894
I wasn't going to make it
harder for any of them here.

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:27.906
Suder did his job when
he was serving with me

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.875
and he's done his job
since he's been on this ship.

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.707
It seems clear
where your investigation

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:34.447
should begin, Lieutenant.

00:08:40.052 --> 00:08:41.644
You wish to see me, Mr. Tuvok?

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:43.484
Sit down.

00:08:46.926 --> 00:08:48.325
You were alone in Engineering

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.294
when Crewman Darwin reported
for duty last night.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:51.455
Yes, sir.

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:52.896
Did you speak to him?

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:55.662
No, we just
sort of looked at each other

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:56.759
and he did
whatever he had to do

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:58.326
and I did what I had to do.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:08:59.701
And what was that?

00:08:59.738 --> 00:09:03.174
I was, um, running
a fuel-consumption analysis

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:05.473
for Lieutenant Torres.

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:08.207
She can tell you.

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:10.738
Are you accusing me
of killing him?

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:16.351
I have accused no one
at this time.

00:09:16.388 --> 00:09:18.356
Did you kill Crewman Darwin?

00:09:19.625 --> 00:09:21.183
No.

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:23.889
No, I barely knew him.

00:09:25.431 --> 00:09:27.797
You know,
just because I'm a Maquis

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:29.232
doesn't make me a killer.

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:32.066
I'll be speaking to everyone
in Engineering...

00:09:32.104 --> 00:09:34.299
perhaps everyone on this ship...

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.604
not just former members
of the Maquis.

00:09:36.642 --> 00:09:39.110
We all know how you feel
about the Maquis.

00:09:39.144 --> 00:09:41.635
I assure you, I have no feelings
about the Maquis.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.648
No, you just spied on us

00:09:43.682 --> 00:09:45.809
and were going to turn us
all over to Starfleet.

00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:48.081
As hard as it may be
for you to understand,

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.884
that did not require
any feelings on my part.

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:57.593
The Doctor places
the time of death at 2214.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.257
Do you remember
what you were doing then?

00:10:00.432 --> 00:10:02.957
I was still running
the fuel analysis.

00:10:03.002 --> 00:10:05.664
I worked on it
until I went off duty.

00:10:05.704 --> 00:10:06.966
Would you be surprised to know

00:10:07.006 --> 00:10:10.407
that your console
was logged off at 2209?

00:10:10.442 --> 00:10:11.807
That's not possible.

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:14.711
Do you have a criminal record,
Mr. Suder?

00:10:14.747 --> 00:10:16.510
Now, that would be

00:10:16.549 --> 00:10:18.346
sort of difficult to check on,
wouldn't it?

00:10:18.384 --> 00:10:20.443
Why would you have
any reason to lie?

00:10:20.486 --> 00:10:22.249
I don't.

00:10:22.288 --> 00:10:24.415
Do you have a criminal record?

00:10:24.456 --> 00:10:25.684
No.

00:10:26.692 --> 00:10:27.681
How would you describe

00:10:27.726 --> 00:10:29.489
your relationship
with Crewman Darwin?

00:10:31.897 --> 00:10:33.797
I had no relationship.

00:10:33.832 --> 00:10:34.799
No disagreements?

00:10:34.833 --> 00:10:35.697
No.

00:10:35.734 --> 00:10:36.701
No fights?

00:10:36.735 --> 00:10:37.724
No.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:38.964
No reason to kill him?

00:10:39.004 --> 00:10:40.164
No.

00:10:40.205 --> 00:10:41.797
You're dismissed, Crewman.

00:10:42.875 --> 00:10:45.241
I may have more questions
for you later.

00:10:52.117 --> 00:10:54.551
Med Lab to Lieutenant Tuvok.

00:10:54.587 --> 00:10:55.679
Go ahead, Doctor.

00:10:55.721 --> 00:10:59.020
I think I've found something
that will help you.

00:10:59.058 --> 00:11:01.618
Do you see the DNA strands
on the lower border?

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:02.854
Yes.

00:11:02.895 --> 00:11:05.261
They were retrieved
from inside the head wound

00:11:05.297 --> 00:11:06.696
by nanites that I designed

00:11:06.732 --> 00:11:09.360
to recognize
unusual DNA patterns.

00:11:09.401 --> 00:11:10.868
This DNA was isolated

00:11:10.903 --> 00:11:12.928
because it didn't belong
to the victim.

00:11:12.972 --> 00:11:15.406
Have you matched it
to a member of the crew?

00:11:19.979 --> 00:11:20.946
Are you certain?

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:23.949
DNA doesn't know how to lie,
Lieutenant.

00:11:33.692 --> 00:11:37.526
I must advise you that
under Starfleet Directive 101,

00:11:37.563 --> 00:11:39.997
you do not have
to answer any questions.

00:11:52.544 --> 00:11:54.102
No.

00:11:55.914 --> 00:11:58.644
No, there's no point
in denying it anymore.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:04.048
Uh...

00:12:04.089 --> 00:12:07.650
I used a two-kilo coil spanner.

00:12:09.395 --> 00:12:14.799
He was sitting at the impulse
system control panel.

00:12:14.833 --> 00:12:17.700
Didn't even look up
when I moved in behind him

00:12:17.736 --> 00:12:22.400
and I swung the spanner
as hard as I could.

00:12:22.441 --> 00:12:24.966
Crewman, I suggest you speak
to counsel.

00:12:25.077 --> 00:12:26.510
There was practically no blood.

00:12:26.545 --> 00:12:28.513
I was surprised at that.

00:12:31.216 --> 00:12:34.242
I figured that the EPS conduit

00:12:34.286 --> 00:12:36.481
was the easiest way
to dispose of the body,

00:12:36.522 --> 00:12:39.116
but... I must have damaged
one of the circuits

00:12:39.158 --> 00:12:41.251
when I put him inside.

00:12:41.293 --> 00:12:43.386
Oh.

00:12:43.429 --> 00:12:48.423
I hid the spanner behind a com
line access panel on Deck 7.

00:12:49.968 --> 00:12:52.061
Why did you kill him, Mr. Suder?

00:13:06.485 --> 00:13:08.510
No reason.

00:13:08.554 --> 00:13:11.955
That is not
a satisfactory answer.

00:13:12.057 --> 00:13:14.150
You must have had some motive.

00:13:17.296 --> 00:13:19.924
I didn't like the way
he looked at me.

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:46.289
No doubt about it.

00:13:46.325 --> 00:13:48.259
This is the murder weapon.

00:13:48.293 --> 00:13:51.091
Mr. Suder is apparently
telling the truth.

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:53.530
You don't seem satisfied,
Lieutenant.

00:13:53.565 --> 00:13:54.623
No.

00:13:54.666 --> 00:13:56.634
You have a confession
and the murder weapon.

00:13:56.668 --> 00:13:58.329
And no established motive.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.735
Does it matter?

00:13:59.772 --> 00:14:02.536
A crime must have
a logical purpose.

00:14:02.574 --> 00:14:05.566
Ah, yes, I see...
how to close the case

00:14:05.611 --> 00:14:08.045
without understanding
the logic of the crime.

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:10.071
For a Vulcan that would
be a dilemma, wouldn't it?

00:14:12.451 --> 00:14:15.943
Doctor, is it possible
that Mr. Suder is psychotic?

00:14:16.021 --> 00:14:17.283
I doubt it.

00:14:17.322 --> 00:14:19.756
Kes, call up
his genetic profile.

00:14:19.792 --> 00:14:22.955
The neuro-genetic markers
are normal.

00:14:23.028 --> 00:14:25.792
There's no tendency
toward bipolar disorder.

00:14:25.831 --> 00:14:28.595
So he's not insane, per se.

00:14:28.634 --> 00:14:31.660
What do the elevated
norepinephrine levels suggest?

00:14:31.703 --> 00:14:34.069
Aggressive, even
violent tendencies.

00:14:34.106 --> 00:14:35.300
Why didn't you report this

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:37.365
immediately after your
examination, Doctor?

00:14:37.409 --> 00:14:39.240
These readings are not
significantly different

00:14:39.278 --> 00:14:41.508
from those of the other
Maquis crewmen.

00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:43.310
Obviously, it takes
a certain personality type

00:14:43.348 --> 00:14:45.748
to be attracted
to the life of an outlaw.

00:14:45.784 --> 00:14:47.979
Don't you believe
his confession, Tuvok?

00:14:48.086 --> 00:14:49.485
In fact, I do.

00:14:49.521 --> 00:14:51.386
Nevertheless, my job
is not finished

00:14:51.423 --> 00:14:52.856
until I determine a motive.

00:14:53.759 --> 00:14:55.954
And what if there was no motive?

00:14:55.994 --> 00:14:58.360
One may not recognize
the motivation,

00:14:58.397 --> 00:15:00.228
but there is always motivation.

00:15:00.265 --> 00:15:01.425
I think you are trapped

00:15:01.466 --> 00:15:03.764
in your own Vulcan logic,
Lieutenant.

00:15:03.802 --> 00:15:05.861
All of us
have violent instincts.

00:15:05.904 --> 00:15:07.872
We have evolved from predators.

00:15:07.906 --> 00:15:09.373
Well, not me, of course.

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:12.036
I've just been programmed
by you predators.

00:15:12.077 --> 00:15:13.738
The question is,
in a civilized world,

00:15:13.779 --> 00:15:15.770
can we suppress those instincts?

00:15:15.814 --> 00:15:17.042
Most of the time, we can.

00:15:17.082 --> 00:15:18.242
Vulcans certainly can.

00:15:18.283 --> 00:15:20.308
You've got your violent feelings

00:15:20.352 --> 00:15:22.820
buried underneath
centuries of control,

00:15:22.855 --> 00:15:24.322
but the rest
of the humanoid races

00:15:24.356 --> 00:15:27.154
aren't always so skilled
at self-discipline.

00:15:27.192 --> 00:15:30.525
Crewman Suder
may have violent impulses

00:15:30.562 --> 00:15:32.052
that he just can't control.

00:15:32.097 --> 00:15:34.497
Do you believe
that a look by Mr. Darwin

00:15:34.533 --> 00:15:36.330
could provoke
such a violent reaction?

00:15:36.368 --> 00:15:38.029
It has been known to happen.

00:15:40.806 --> 00:15:43.070
I do not accept
that explanation.

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:54.951
I already told you
why I killed him, Lieutenant.

00:15:54.987 --> 00:15:56.716
You didn't like
the way he looked at you.

00:15:56.755 --> 00:15:57.722
Right.

00:15:57.756 --> 00:15:59.656
Just how did he look at you?

00:15:59.691 --> 00:16:02.421
Like a lot of people
in Starfleet do.

00:16:02.461 --> 00:16:04.622
So this murder
could in fact be explained

00:16:04.663 --> 00:16:07.131
as an outburst of rage
against Starfleet.

00:16:09.334 --> 00:16:12.826
Look, if that's how you
want to look at this...

00:16:12.871 --> 00:16:14.805
I want the truth.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:18.241
I don't like Starfleet.

00:16:18.277 --> 00:16:20.905
I won't deny that.

00:16:22.114 --> 00:16:23.308
But...

00:16:23.348 --> 00:16:24.815
Yes?

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:28.479
I have killed people
who weren't in Starfleet

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:29.646
for the same reason...

00:16:29.688 --> 00:16:32.816
I did not like the way
they looked at me.

00:16:32.858 --> 00:16:36.419
I've thought about
killing you, Lieutenant.

00:16:36.461 --> 00:16:41.956
In my case, you have a motive...
my previous mission as a spy,

00:16:42.034 --> 00:16:45.435
my role as your accuser...
but to my knowledge,

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:47.529
Crewman Darwin had
done nothing to you.

00:16:47.572 --> 00:16:49.699
That's true.

00:16:49.741 --> 00:16:51.971
Then why choose him as a victim?

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:54.205
I don't know.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.180
Do you feel remorse?

00:16:59.384 --> 00:17:02.911
I don't seem to feel anything
at all.

00:17:02.988 --> 00:17:07.618
Most Betazoids can sense
other people's emotions...

00:17:09.361 --> 00:17:12.421
I can't even sense my own.

00:17:12.464 --> 00:17:15.133
So what's going to happen
to me now?

00:17:15.266 --> 00:17:17.063
I'll have to discuss that
with the Captain.

00:17:18.803 --> 00:17:21.465
I know what I'd do
if I were her.

00:17:25.243 --> 00:17:27.370
Guess I'm lucky.

00:17:27.411 --> 00:17:30.346
The Federation
doesn't execute people.

00:18:06.584 --> 00:18:08.347
It is important
that I understand

00:18:08.386 --> 00:18:10.115
why you killed Mr. Darwin.

00:18:11.789 --> 00:18:13.916
I wish I could help you,
Lieutenant.

00:18:13.991 --> 00:18:15.049
You can...

00:18:15.092 --> 00:18:18.220
and indirectly, I may be able
to help you, as well.

00:18:18.262 --> 00:18:20.025
Do you know what a mind-meld is?

00:18:21.232 --> 00:18:22.699
It's that...

00:18:22.733 --> 00:18:25.930
Vulcan thing where you
grab someone's head.

00:18:26.003 --> 00:18:28.335
We would be
telepathically linked...

00:18:28.372 --> 00:18:30.272
exchanging our thoughts...

00:18:30.308 --> 00:18:33.436
in essence, becoming one mind.

00:18:33.477 --> 00:18:35.707
One mind? You and me?

00:18:35.746 --> 00:18:37.907
I wouldn't recommend that,
Lieutenant.

00:18:37.949 --> 00:18:39.610
It is not without risk,

00:18:39.650 --> 00:18:42.210
but as a Vulcan,
I have internal processes

00:18:42.253 --> 00:18:44.949
that allow me
to control violent instincts.

00:18:45.022 --> 00:18:46.887
I believe I will
be able to suppress

00:18:46.924 --> 00:18:49.154
whatever feelings
I draw from you.

00:18:49.193 --> 00:18:52.162
And how will I be helped
by all this?

00:18:52.196 --> 00:18:55.495
It is likely that you will gain,
at least for a time,

00:18:55.533 --> 00:18:57.501
some of my self-discipline

00:18:57.535 --> 00:18:59.867
to better control
your own violent nature.

00:19:06.344 --> 00:19:08.335
What do I have to do?

00:19:09.547 --> 00:19:11.014
Release the force field.

00:19:25.763 --> 00:19:29.199
My mind to your mind...

00:19:29.233 --> 00:19:32.361
your thoughts to my thoughts...

00:19:42.046 --> 00:19:43.877
Radiogenic particle density

00:19:43.914 --> 00:19:48.442
at the measured coordinates
was 1873 per cubic meter.

00:19:49.954 --> 00:19:54.550
And the winner
of 16 replicator rations

00:19:54.592 --> 00:19:57.755
in the Paris radiogenic
sweepstakes is...

00:19:57.795 --> 00:19:58.762
- Shh.
- Shh.

00:19:58.796 --> 00:19:59.763
Computer?

00:19:59.797 --> 00:20:01.822
There is no winner today.

00:20:01.866 --> 00:20:04.426
What? No winner?

00:20:04.468 --> 00:20:06.902
Computer, are you positive?

00:20:06.937 --> 00:20:08.529
Try your luck again.

00:20:08.572 --> 00:20:11.097
Tomorrow you could be a winner.

00:20:11.142 --> 00:20:12.769
Very funny.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:13.834
You heard the little lady.

00:20:13.878 --> 00:20:15.743
Try your luck again, folks.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:18.647
The pot grows daily
until we have a winner.

00:20:18.683 --> 00:20:21.243
Enter your name on the
padd and pick a number.

00:20:21.285 --> 00:20:23.480
Can I buy you lunch, Mr. Kim?

00:20:23.521 --> 00:20:25.648
I have an extra ration today.

00:20:25.690 --> 00:20:27.419
Two, by my count.

00:20:27.458 --> 00:20:29.153
Ten percent of the day's action.

00:20:29.193 --> 00:20:31.889
The only one who wins
every day is you.

00:20:31.929 --> 00:20:34.693
I think I'll have
some prime rib...

00:20:34.732 --> 00:20:36.199
medium rare...

00:20:36.233 --> 00:20:38.861
mashed potatoes,
creamed spinach.

00:20:38.903 --> 00:20:41.167
And maybe
some Yorkshire pudding...

00:20:41.205 --> 00:20:43.935
and a raktajino
with whipped cream on top.

00:20:43.974 --> 00:20:45.874
...so it ultimately turned out

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:48.936
to be a worthwhile
and enlightening experience.

00:20:48.979 --> 00:20:52.642
Did you get any of the answers
you were after?

00:20:52.683 --> 00:20:54.947
It is difficult for me
to accept, Captain,

00:20:54.985 --> 00:20:58.512
but Mr. Suder was telling
the truth as he knew it.

00:20:58.556 --> 00:21:02.253
He is a man with an
incredibly violent nature,

00:21:02.293 --> 00:21:03.555
living in an environment

00:21:03.594 --> 00:21:05.357
without any outlet
to express it.

00:21:05.396 --> 00:21:07.830
I am surprised he was able
to maintain his self-control

00:21:07.865 --> 00:21:08.854
for as long as he did.

00:21:08.899 --> 00:21:10.628
I guess in his earlier life,

00:21:10.668 --> 00:21:12.829
he always found ways
to release those impulses...

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:15.202
like volunteering
for the Maquis.

00:21:15.239 --> 00:21:16.831
What do we do with him?

00:21:17.842 --> 00:21:20.140
If we were home,
he'd be sent to prison.

00:21:20.177 --> 00:21:23.305
The brig is the closest thing
we have,

00:21:23.347 --> 00:21:25.144
but I don't think
we can just leave him

00:21:25.182 --> 00:21:27.275
down in our dungeon
for the rest of the trip.

00:21:27.318 --> 00:21:28.979
Nor would it be appropriate

00:21:29.086 --> 00:21:31.816
to leave him in the custody
of someone in this Quadrant.

00:21:31.856 --> 00:21:33.414
I agree.

00:21:33.457 --> 00:21:36.255
Captain...

00:21:36.293 --> 00:21:39.490
he is prepared
to die for his crime.

00:21:44.668 --> 00:21:47.102
An execution?

00:21:47.138 --> 00:21:49.368
You're not seriously
suggesting that we...

00:21:49.407 --> 00:21:50.396
I only mention it

00:21:50.441 --> 00:21:52.204
because of the extenuating
circumstances

00:21:52.243 --> 00:21:55.701
and because he feels it would be
an appropriate punishment.

00:21:55.746 --> 00:21:56.906
I don't.

00:21:56.947 --> 00:21:59.609
I prefer to rehabilitate him,
not to end his life.

00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:02.380
We'll confine him to quarters.

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:05.218
Work with Kim to install
maximum-security containment.

00:22:05.256 --> 00:22:06.245
Pardon me, Captain,

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:09.555
but allowing him the comfort
of his own quarters

00:22:09.593 --> 00:22:12.187
doesn't seem an appropriate
punishment for murder.

00:22:14.298 --> 00:22:15.890
If we don't get home soon,

00:22:15.933 --> 00:22:19.061
he'll be in that room
a long time, Mr. Tuvok.

00:22:19.103 --> 00:22:21.128
I think this is
the best we can do

00:22:21.172 --> 00:22:22.799
under these circumstances.

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:27.334
Crewman Darwin's three sisters
might not agree.

00:22:33.584 --> 00:22:36.178
How is Suder
since the mind-meld?

00:22:36.220 --> 00:22:39.212
Quite calm and controlled.

00:22:39.256 --> 00:22:40.814
Clearly, the meld initiated

00:22:40.858 --> 00:22:43.224
some high cortical activity
in his brain.

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:46.320
And you, Tuvok,
any adverse effects?

00:22:46.363 --> 00:22:47.591
I will admit

00:22:47.631 --> 00:22:50.361
that I am more disconcerted
than I anticipated.

00:22:50.401 --> 00:22:53.131
Why don't you take a day
or two off for meditation?

00:22:53.170 --> 00:22:55.764
Thank you,
but I am already taking steps

00:22:55.806 --> 00:22:57.865
to purge
these residual feelings.

00:22:57.908 --> 00:23:00.433
I don't believe time off
will be necessary.

00:23:00.478 --> 00:23:04.141
I will, of course, advise you
of any further complications.

00:23:05.816 --> 00:23:07.078
Tuvok.

00:23:10.087 --> 00:23:11.850
Take care of yourself.

00:23:31.342 --> 00:23:33.708
I would prefer to be alone.

00:23:33.744 --> 00:23:34.768
Okay. All right.

00:23:34.812 --> 00:23:37.144
Far be it from me
to bother anyone.

00:23:37.181 --> 00:23:40.708
If you really want me to leave,
I'll leave.

00:23:40.751 --> 00:23:43.117
I really want you to leave.

00:23:43.153 --> 00:23:44.677
I don't believe you.

00:23:44.722 --> 00:23:47.122
Your voice says "go away,"

00:23:47.157 --> 00:23:49.284
but your heart wants me
to make you smile.

00:23:50.528 --> 00:23:53.725
Please, go away.

00:23:53.764 --> 00:23:57.495
Come on... a little smile.

00:23:57.535 --> 00:23:59.264
How is it going to hurt?

00:23:59.303 --> 00:24:01.828
I won't tell anyone.

00:24:01.872 --> 00:24:04.568
What must I do
to convince you to stop?

00:24:04.608 --> 00:24:07.168
Come on. Just a little,
itty-bitty smile.

00:24:07.211 --> 00:24:10.044
Just let the mouth
curl a little there.

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:12.173
That's...

00:24:12.216 --> 00:24:14.184
There's an old Talaxian song

00:24:14.218 --> 00:24:16.379
my mother used
to sing me as a child.

00:24:16.420 --> 00:24:18.479
I'm going to sing it to you
every day

00:24:18.522 --> 00:24:20.046
from now on.
It goes...

00:24:22.159 --> 00:24:24.127
Mr. Vulcan, I...

00:24:24.161 --> 00:24:25.594
Oh, I can't breath...

00:24:26.430 --> 00:24:28.591
Can't... I can't breath...

00:24:28.632 --> 00:24:31.123
I'm sorry if I...

00:24:45.883 --> 00:24:49.219
Computer, end holodeck program.

00:25:01.531 --> 00:25:03.226
Particle density

00:25:03.266 --> 00:25:06.895
at the measured coordinates
was 1415 per cubic meter.

00:25:06.936 --> 00:25:08.563
And the winner is?

00:25:10.240 --> 00:25:11.605
Computer?

00:25:13.176 --> 00:25:14.370
Computer?

00:25:14.410 --> 00:25:16.469
There won't be any more winners.

00:25:22.452 --> 00:25:24.579
Oh, come on, Chakotay.

00:25:24.621 --> 00:25:26.816
We were just having
a little fun.

00:25:26.856 --> 00:25:29.518
The recreational facilities
of the Delta Quadrant

00:25:29.559 --> 00:25:30.651
being what they are.

00:25:30.693 --> 00:25:32.957
I've heard you're responsible
for this, Lieutenant.

00:25:34.163 --> 00:25:36.688
I didn't think Starfleet
would have a problem with it.

00:25:36.733 --> 00:25:39.258
With a senior officer
running a gambling operation

00:25:39.302 --> 00:25:41.293
and skimming profits
from each day's proceeds?

00:25:41.337 --> 00:25:43.999
Now, why would Starfleet
have a problem with that?

00:25:45.408 --> 00:25:47.706
Since you all seem to have
extra replicator rations,

00:25:47.744 --> 00:25:49.075
you won't be needing these.

00:25:49.112 --> 00:25:51.080
Today's pot is hereby
confiscated.

00:25:54.484 --> 00:25:56.850
The Captain's put a lot
of faith in you, Mr. Paris.

00:25:56.886 --> 00:25:58.285
She'll be disappointed.

00:25:59.589 --> 00:26:01.580
You're on report.

00:26:01.624 --> 00:26:05.082
Now, there's a tough job...

00:26:05.128 --> 00:26:07.028
filling out reports.

00:26:07.063 --> 00:26:10.123
But somebody's got to do it.

00:26:17.073 --> 00:26:18.131
Thanks a lot.

00:26:35.591 --> 00:26:38.151
I did not hear you come in,
Lieutenant.

00:26:38.194 --> 00:26:40.185
How are you feeling?

00:26:43.700 --> 00:26:44.962
Centered.

00:26:45.068 --> 00:26:46.763
Don't be misled.

00:26:46.803 --> 00:26:48.964
Your violent instincts
still exist.

00:26:49.005 --> 00:26:50.973
You are simply suppressing
them as Vulcans do.

00:26:51.074 --> 00:26:53.474
I can feel the difference.

00:26:53.509 --> 00:26:57.570
It is almost as if I can observe
the violence inside me

00:26:57.613 --> 00:27:00.138
without letting it
get too close.

00:27:00.183 --> 00:27:01.810
It is quite remarkable

00:27:01.851 --> 00:27:04.547
what you Vulcans
have learned to do.

00:27:05.788 --> 00:27:08.552
Understand that this will
not be a permanent change,

00:27:08.591 --> 00:27:11.424
unless you commit
to a strict daily regime

00:27:11.461 --> 00:27:14.521
of meditation
and mental exercise.

00:27:14.564 --> 00:27:18.125
I also believe that a series
of holodeck programs

00:27:18.167 --> 00:27:20.294
designed to allow
your violent tendencies

00:27:20.336 --> 00:27:22.600
to be released
in a safe environment

00:27:22.638 --> 00:27:25.300
may help to purge
your aggressive impulses.

00:27:26.342 --> 00:27:31.302
Holographic violence
does not give the same...

00:27:31.347 --> 00:27:33.110
sensation as the real thing.

00:27:33.149 --> 00:27:34.275
I've tried it.

00:27:34.317 --> 00:27:37.946
Has anyone ever suggested
targeted neuro-synaptic therapy?

00:27:38.955 --> 00:27:40.422
That didn't work either.

00:27:40.456 --> 00:27:43.357
Our Doctor is programmed
with the medical knowledge

00:27:43.393 --> 00:27:44.655
of every Federation world.

00:27:44.694 --> 00:27:47.561
Perhaps he'll know of some
treatment you haven't tried.

00:27:47.597 --> 00:27:53.160
Since the meld, I feel capable
of controlling myself.

00:27:53.202 --> 00:27:56.262
Perhaps with your help,
I can learn to stay this way.

00:27:59.809 --> 00:28:02.505
It must be difficult for you.

00:28:11.053 --> 00:28:12.918
Difficult?

00:28:12.955 --> 00:28:16.015
Knowing violence
as I've known it.

00:28:16.058 --> 00:28:19.755
I have studied violence
for over 100 years.

00:28:19.796 --> 00:28:20.922
Studying it

00:28:20.997 --> 00:28:23.431
and knowing it are two
different things, aren't they?

00:28:26.302 --> 00:28:28.327
It's attractive, isn't it?

00:28:30.206 --> 00:28:32.299
Attractive?

00:28:32.341 --> 00:28:34.332
Violence.

00:28:34.377 --> 00:28:36.402
On the contrary.

00:28:36.446 --> 00:28:38.846
I find it disturbing.

00:28:38.881 --> 00:28:39.939
You're right.

00:28:39.982 --> 00:28:41.813
It is disturbing...

00:28:41.851 --> 00:28:44.149
never knowing
when that impulse may come,

00:28:44.187 --> 00:28:46.451
or whether or not
you can control it when it does.

00:28:46.489 --> 00:28:48.923
You live on the edge
of every moment

00:28:48.958 --> 00:28:53.691
and yet, in its own way,
violence is attractive, too.

00:28:53.729 --> 00:28:57.392
Maybe because it
doesn't require logic.

00:28:57.433 --> 00:29:00.869
Perhaps that's why
it's so liberating.

00:29:00.903 --> 00:29:03.895
Ironic, isn't it...

00:29:04.006 --> 00:29:06.406
that I can share with you,
of all people,

00:29:06.442 --> 00:29:09.741
what I have hidden from everyone
all my life.

00:29:11.981 --> 00:29:13.915
Can we do it again, Tuvok?

00:29:15.418 --> 00:29:17.181
Again?

00:29:17.220 --> 00:29:18.448
Meld.

00:29:21.057 --> 00:29:23.218
That would not be advisable.

00:29:25.862 --> 00:29:27.989
I understand.

00:29:29.298 --> 00:29:31.732
Really, I do.

00:29:31.767 --> 00:29:35.134
I have thought about it a lot.

00:29:35.171 --> 00:29:40.438
In a way, a mind-meld is almost
an act of violence, isn't it?

00:29:40.476 --> 00:29:42.273
I don't understand
why you would...

00:29:42.311 --> 00:29:43.278
Penetration.

00:29:43.312 --> 00:29:45.712
Your will dissolving mine.

00:29:45.748 --> 00:29:47.477
The joining.

00:29:47.517 --> 00:29:50.384
It seems to me that a mind-meld

00:29:50.419 --> 00:29:53.286
might be fatal
if you lost control.

00:30:06.168 --> 00:30:10.070
Computer, place level-1
security seals on this room.

00:30:10.106 --> 00:30:13.371
Acknowledged.
Security seals in place.

00:30:13.409 --> 00:30:18.108
Delete security clearance:
Tuvok-one-four-nine-four-lambda.

00:30:18.147 --> 00:30:21.275
Specified security clearance
deleted.

00:30:23.019 --> 00:30:24.987
Please inform the Captain

00:30:25.021 --> 00:30:26.989
that I am no longer
fit for duty.

00:30:27.089 --> 00:30:28.852
Acknowledged.

00:30:38.501 --> 00:30:40.128
Computer, lift the security seal

00:30:40.169 --> 00:30:41.261
from Lieutenant Tuvok's
quarters.

00:30:44.240 --> 00:30:46.265
Wait here.

00:30:57.453 --> 00:31:00.115
I would advise you
not to enter, Captain.

00:31:08.064 --> 00:31:09.429
Tuvok.

00:31:09.465 --> 00:31:12.798
Please, do not come any closer.

00:31:19.909 --> 00:31:21.137
Talk to me.

00:31:21.177 --> 00:31:22.144
I said...

00:31:22.178 --> 00:31:24.271
don't come any closer.

00:31:26.415 --> 00:31:28.246
We need to get you to Sick Bay.

00:31:30.319 --> 00:31:32.549
It would be safer for the crew

00:31:32.588 --> 00:31:35.523
if I were to remain
in these quarters.

00:31:36.892 --> 00:31:40.726
I remind you, I am trained
in the martial arts

00:31:40.763 --> 00:31:43.698
of many Alpha Quadrant cultures.

00:31:43.733 --> 00:31:46.201
Sitting here,
attempting to meditate,

00:31:46.235 --> 00:31:48.567
I have counted
the number of ways

00:31:48.604 --> 00:31:50.902
I know of killing someone

00:31:50.940 --> 00:31:54.967
using just a finger, a hand...

00:31:55.011 --> 00:31:56.569
a foot...

00:31:57.813 --> 00:32:01.340
I had reached 94
when you entered.

00:32:01.384 --> 00:32:05.184
The Doctor is fully versed
in Vulcan medicine.

00:32:17.433 --> 00:32:20.300
Again, for safety reasons,

00:32:20.336 --> 00:32:25.035
I recommend you sedate me
before you initiate transport.

00:32:28.110 --> 00:32:30.977
Levels of neuropeptides
in the limbic system

00:32:31.013 --> 00:32:32.275
are down 15 percent.

00:32:34.183 --> 00:32:36.549
There's a definite
neuro-chemical imbalance

00:32:36.585 --> 00:32:38.075
in the mesiofrontal cortex.

00:32:38.120 --> 00:32:39.144
Which means what?

00:32:39.188 --> 00:32:40.348
That's where the Vulcan

00:32:40.389 --> 00:32:42.357
psycho-suppression
systems are located.

00:32:42.391 --> 00:32:45.690
This may be the result
of a incompatibility

00:32:45.728 --> 00:32:47.559
with the Betazoid
telepathic neural center.

00:32:47.596 --> 00:32:49.086
I'm not sure.

00:32:52.201 --> 00:32:55.568
Vulcan mind-melds...

00:32:55.604 --> 00:32:57.094
utter foolishness.

00:32:57.139 --> 00:32:58.538
Anybody with an ounce of sense

00:32:58.574 --> 00:33:01.099
wouldn't share his brain
with someone else.

00:33:01.143 --> 00:33:03.634
Would you?
I certainly wouldn't.

00:33:03.679 --> 00:33:06.045
And of course,
when something goes wrong...

00:33:06.082 --> 00:33:07.572
and believe me,
it does more often

00:33:07.616 --> 00:33:08.844
than they'd like to admit...

00:33:08.884 --> 00:33:10.852
the first thing
they call out is, "Doctor?"

00:33:10.886 --> 00:33:12.080
Can you help him?

00:33:12.121 --> 00:33:13.110
I wish I could tell you.

00:33:13.155 --> 00:33:14.782
There's a recommended
course of treatments

00:33:14.824 --> 00:33:15.813
that should begin immediately.

00:33:15.858 --> 00:33:17.057
What does it involve?

00:33:17.190 --> 00:33:18.088
First, we have to take away

00:33:18.124 --> 00:33:20.115
his ability to control
his violence.

00:33:20.160 --> 00:33:22.355
We do this in short bursts
over a period of time

00:33:22.395 --> 00:33:24.693
and hope it provides
a shock to his system.

00:33:24.731 --> 00:33:26.255
If it works,

00:33:26.299 --> 00:33:29.234
his own neural controls
will take over again.

00:33:32.672 --> 00:33:34.936
I believe we're about ready.

00:33:35.942 --> 00:33:37.273
Revive him.

00:33:48.388 --> 00:33:49.821
Something has changed.

00:33:49.856 --> 00:33:50.982
We've temporarily

00:33:51.024 --> 00:33:53.322
removed all of your
emotional suppression

00:33:53.359 --> 00:33:54.621
abilities, Lieutenant.

00:33:54.661 --> 00:33:55.650
How do you feel?

00:33:58.198 --> 00:34:01.463
I... feel.

00:34:01.501 --> 00:34:04.937
Tuvok,
do you know where you are?

00:34:08.341 --> 00:34:10.571
Of course I know
where I am, Captain.

00:34:10.610 --> 00:34:15.946
I'm just not sure I know...
who I am.

00:34:15.982 --> 00:34:17.347
Try to relax.

00:34:17.383 --> 00:34:20.375
The treatment still has
about three minutes to go.

00:34:21.754 --> 00:34:23.654
Oh, it must be working

00:34:23.690 --> 00:34:28.457
because I feel very strong.

00:34:28.495 --> 00:34:33.159
Very... powerful.

00:34:34.167 --> 00:34:36.067
Quite euphoric.

00:34:36.102 --> 00:34:38.900
This must be
how my ancestors felt.

00:34:38.938 --> 00:34:41.304
Doctor, would you
consider allowing me

00:34:41.341 --> 00:34:43.275
to remain this way for a while?

00:34:43.309 --> 00:34:45.140
It would be
a valuable opportunity

00:34:45.178 --> 00:34:46.805
for me to study
primal Vulcan behavior.

00:34:46.846 --> 00:34:48.575
Sorry, I'm not prepared
to do that.

00:34:48.615 --> 00:34:51.106
The course of treatment
is very specific.

00:34:51.151 --> 00:34:54.245
You are not invulnerable,
hologram.

00:34:54.287 --> 00:34:56.517
A few well-chosen commands

00:34:56.556 --> 00:34:59.252
to the computer,
and you will cease to exist.

00:35:03.163 --> 00:35:05.597
Two minutes, 30 seconds left.

00:35:05.632 --> 00:35:07.725
You look shocked, Captain.

00:35:09.135 --> 00:35:13.936
You must be asking yourself,
"What if this doesn't work?

00:35:13.973 --> 00:35:16.464
What do we do then?"

00:35:17.977 --> 00:35:19.842
I have an idea.

00:35:19.879 --> 00:35:24.077
I'll just stay in my quarters
for the rest of the trip.

00:35:24.117 --> 00:35:26.608
I'll just relax

00:35:26.653 --> 00:35:28.382
and read,

00:35:28.421 --> 00:35:30.321
eat the ship's food,

00:35:30.356 --> 00:35:32.586
use the ship's energy,

00:35:32.625 --> 00:35:34.490
all in the comforts
of my own room.

00:35:35.495 --> 00:35:37.429
Why, even Mr. Suder and I
could get together

00:35:37.463 --> 00:35:39.124
for a few hands
of Cardassian pinochle

00:35:39.165 --> 00:35:40.462
once or twice a week.

00:35:40.500 --> 00:35:42.331
That is how we treat
violent offenders

00:35:42.368 --> 00:35:43.494
on this ship, isn't it?

00:35:43.536 --> 00:35:46.198
You are not
a violent offender, Tuvok.

00:35:46.239 --> 00:35:47.433
I could be.

00:35:47.473 --> 00:35:49.907
Just like Suder.

00:35:49.943 --> 00:35:53.435
You know, Captain,
I don't mind telling you

00:35:53.479 --> 00:35:56.710
something the other Tuvok
never would.

00:35:56.749 --> 00:35:59.445
You are wrong.

00:35:59.485 --> 00:36:02.784
Sparing Suder's life
is a sign of weakness.

00:36:04.557 --> 00:36:06.354
You disgust me.

00:36:09.329 --> 00:36:11.524
All you humans do.

00:36:11.564 --> 00:36:13.759
Admit it.

00:36:13.800 --> 00:36:17.429
Part of you feels as I do.

00:36:17.470 --> 00:36:20.462
Part of you wants him to die
for what he did.

00:36:20.506 --> 00:36:22.235
No part of me feels that way.

00:36:22.275 --> 00:36:23.833
Liar!

00:36:23.876 --> 00:36:28.336
He has killed
and you know he deserves to die!

00:36:30.116 --> 00:36:32.550
On behalf
of the victim's family, Captain,

00:36:32.585 --> 00:36:34.712
I beg you to reconsider.

00:36:34.754 --> 00:36:38.815
Give them the satisfaction
of his execution.

00:36:45.331 --> 00:36:47.959
I have a radical suggestion,
Captain.

00:36:49.435 --> 00:36:52.268
Release the force field...

00:36:52.305 --> 00:36:55.035
and I'll kill him for you.

00:36:59.679 --> 00:37:01.442
Release the force field.

00:37:07.920 --> 00:37:08.887
My student...

00:37:08.921 --> 00:37:10.149
my protégé...

00:37:12.659 --> 00:37:13.921
there is so much to learn

00:37:13.960 --> 00:37:16.190
for each of us today,
isn't there?

00:37:16.229 --> 00:37:18.094
You'll be all right, Tuvok.

00:37:18.131 --> 00:37:20.031
This'll be over in 30 seconds.

00:37:20.066 --> 00:37:21.761
Listen to what I tell you.

00:37:21.801 --> 00:37:23.928
Release the force field.

00:37:25.905 --> 00:37:27.133
I'm sorry.

00:37:27.173 --> 00:37:29.733
I had them disable
your telepathic abilities, too.

00:37:29.776 --> 00:37:31.767
You can't reach me, Tuvok.

00:37:31.811 --> 00:37:34.678
Release the force field!

00:37:37.784 --> 00:37:39.376
Ten seconds.

00:37:44.390 --> 00:37:45.584
Five seconds.

00:37:51.998 --> 00:37:53.260
It's over.

00:37:53.299 --> 00:37:55.859
He's lost consciousness.

00:37:55.902 --> 00:37:57.199
He might be able
to fool the sensors.

00:37:57.236 --> 00:37:58.828
Sedate him again.

00:37:58.871 --> 00:38:01.499
Computer,
remove the force field.

00:38:03.876 --> 00:38:05.707
Help me get him back on the bed.

00:38:09.682 --> 00:38:11.707
How many treatments do you think
will be necessary?

00:38:11.751 --> 00:38:13.742
I wish I knew, Captain.

00:38:13.786 --> 00:38:16.152
In a sense, Mr. Tuvok's
mind is fighting

00:38:16.189 --> 00:38:18.487
a classic battle
between good and evil.

00:38:18.524 --> 00:38:22.119
The battle may be won
in a day, a year...

00:38:22.161 --> 00:38:24.391
or it may never be won.

00:40:05.097 --> 00:40:06.655
Tuvok?

00:40:18.144 --> 00:40:20.442
I wondered what happened to you.

00:40:20.480 --> 00:40:22.175
They wouldn't tell me anything.

00:40:22.215 --> 00:40:26.174
There were some complications
from the meld.

00:40:26.219 --> 00:40:28.744
I wondered about that.

00:40:28.788 --> 00:40:30.983
I've been undergoing

00:40:31.023 --> 00:40:33.491
neuro-synaptic therapy
in Sick Bay.

00:40:33.526 --> 00:40:35.687
It didn't work.

00:40:36.729 --> 00:40:38.356
No.

00:40:43.703 --> 00:40:45.603
Have you come to kill me?

00:40:45.638 --> 00:40:48.402
To execute you for your crime.

00:40:48.441 --> 00:40:51.205
To execute me?

00:40:51.244 --> 00:40:53.371
I see.

00:40:53.412 --> 00:40:56.848
And calling it that makes it
more comfortable for you.

00:40:56.883 --> 00:40:58.748
I will take no comfort in this.

00:41:01.954 --> 00:41:05.890
A most logical use of violence...
to punish the violent.

00:41:10.062 --> 00:41:13.725
We both know
that I am prepared to die,

00:41:13.766 --> 00:41:16.064
but are you prepared to kill?

00:41:16.102 --> 00:41:18.263
It needs to be done.

00:41:18.304 --> 00:41:20.966
To release
your violent impulses?

00:41:21.073 --> 00:41:22.472
To serve justice.

00:41:22.508 --> 00:41:24.339
Justice or vengeance?

00:41:24.377 --> 00:41:27.175
Understand one thing, Tuvok.

00:41:27.213 --> 00:41:28.305
I can promise you

00:41:28.347 --> 00:41:31.578
this will not
silence your demons.

00:41:31.617 --> 00:41:33.710
If you can't control
the violence,

00:41:33.753 --> 00:41:36.119
the violence controls you.

00:41:36.155 --> 00:41:39.716
Be prepared to yield
your entire being to it,

00:41:39.759 --> 00:41:42.922
to sacrifice your place
in civilized life,

00:41:42.962 --> 00:41:45.863
for you will no longer
be a part of it

00:41:45.898 --> 00:41:48.332
and there's no return.

00:41:50.036 --> 00:41:51.526
I...

00:41:51.571 --> 00:41:53.334
seek...

00:41:53.372 --> 00:41:54.396
no return.

00:41:54.440 --> 00:41:55.407
Of course.

00:41:55.441 --> 00:41:56.999
You would not be able
to live with yourself.

00:41:57.043 --> 00:41:58.840
Then we are both to die,

00:41:58.878 --> 00:42:01.278
and that will end the torment.

00:42:01.314 --> 00:42:04.772
My mind...
to your mind.

00:42:04.817 --> 00:42:06.842
My thoughts...

00:42:06.886 --> 00:42:08.683
to your thoughts.

00:42:10.623 --> 00:42:11.922
My mind...

00:42:12.055 --> 00:42:13.852
to your mind.

00:42:13.890 --> 00:42:18.725
My thoughts to your thoughts.

00:42:51.962 --> 00:42:53.930
Crewman Suder to the Bridge.

00:42:53.964 --> 00:42:55.932
Suder, what are you doing
with a combadge?

00:42:55.966 --> 00:42:58.332
You better get down here,
Chakotay.

00:42:58.368 --> 00:43:00.802
Lieutenant Tuvok needs help.
